---
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import MobilityBlueprintTheme from '../components/MobilityBlueprintTheme.astro';
import MobilitySystemPlate from '../components/MobilitySystemPlate.astro';
import concept from '../data/mobility-2030.json';
import regulatory from '../data/mobility-2030-regulatory.json';
import '../styles/mobility-manufacturing.css';
const source = (id: string) => regulatory.sources.find(s => s.id === id)!;
const description = 'Three Hoydich Enterprises personal-transit design studies, an El Segundo manufacturing vision, system architecture and staged research roadmap. 2030 design fiction.';
---
<BlockLayout title="Hoydich Enterprises · Mobility 2030" description={description} hideAds showNetworkStrip={false} image="/images/mobility-2030/stratus-two-seat.webp" imageWidth={1672} imageHeight={941} alternates={[{type:'application/json',href:'/mobility-2030.json',title:'Mobility concept and research data'}]}>
<div class="blueprint">
  <nav class="bp-nav" aria-label="Feature navigation"><a href="/">← PointCast</a><span><a href="/manufacturing/">Manufacturing atlas ↗</a><a href="/mobility-2030.json">JSON</a><MobilityBlueprintTheme/></span></nav>
  <header class="bp-hero"><p class="bp-kicker">Hoydich Enterprises / 2030 design study / El Segundo</p><h1>Beyond the car.<br/>Built around the person.</h1><p class="bp-intro">Three personal-transit concepts, a local manufacturing thesis, and the evidence gates between imagination and a real program.</p><p class="bp-notice">{concept.disclaimer}</p></header>
  <figure class="bp-plate"><img src="/images/mobility-2030/stratus-two-seat.webp" width="1672" height="941" alt={concept.forms[1].alt} fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>STRATUS / 2030 design study. Original generated concept art. Neither performance nor certification is established. The depicted coastal hangar is fictional.</figcaption></figure>
  <nav class="bp-tabs" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#forms">Three forms</a><a href="#architecture">System architecture</a><a href="#factory">Factory vision</a><a href="#roadmap">Research & capital</a><a href="#approval">Approval paths</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
  <section class="bp-section" id="forms"><p class="bp-number">01 / The design space</p><h2>A cabin. A craft. A cocoon.</h2><p>{concept.premise} The images propose shapes and experiences; they do not resolve mechanics, occupant protection or aircraft classification.</p><div class="bp-grid">{concept.forms.map(form=><article class="bp-card"><p class="bp-kicker">2030 design study</p><h3>{form.name}</h3><p>{form.subtitle}</p><figure class="bp-plate"><img src={'/images/mobility-2030/'+form.image} width="1672" height="941" alt={form.alt} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{form.caption}</figcaption></figure><p>{form.body}</p><p class="bp-small">Open question: {form.uncertainty}</p></article>)}<article class="bp-card"><p class="bp-kicker">Design rule / Start with a person</p><h3>Useful before airborne.</h3><p>First learn whether the ground cabin improves a real journey: boarding, storage, service and understandable controls. A separable aerial carrier is an unresolved hypothesis, not a commercial dependency.</p><p>Accessibility, maintenance and community acceptance belong in the first drawing. A beautiful canopy or shroud in a render is not evidence of safety.</p><p class="bp-small">No range, speed, lift, payload, autonomy, noise or production-price claim is made.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="bp-section" id="architecture"><p class="bp-number">02 / Conceptual architecture</p><h2>Give every interface an owner.</h2><MobilitySystemPlate/><figure class="bp-plate"><img src="/images/mobility-2030/systems-concept-plate.webp" width="1672" height="941" alt="Cobalt blueprint-style exploded illustration of conceptual groups in a two-seat personal aircraft." loading="lazy"/><figcaption>BP.02 / Non-dimensional concept illustration. Separated forms are functional groups, not a parts list, assembly sequence or validated load path.</figcaption></figure><div class="bp-grid">{concept.systems.map((system,i)=><article class="bp-card"><p class="bp-number">SYS.{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</p><h3>{system.name}</h3><p>{system.role}</p><dl><dt>Interface to resolve</dt><dd>{system.interfaces}</dd><dt>Evidence before advancing</dt><dd>{system.evidence}</dd></dl></article>)}</div><p class="bp-notice">Shared ground and aviation hardware is a hypothesis. Road compliance does not qualify a part for flight. Ground propulsion and braking, aviation propulsion, flight controls and navigation, module retention, production quality, training and service each need their own reviewed requirements.</p></section>
  <section class="bp-section" id="factory"><p class="bp-number">03 / El Segundo manufacturing vision</p><h2>A studio that can become a factory.</h2><p>A proposed El Segundo design, integration and service center, supported by qualified regional suppliers. There is no acquired facility, capacity commitment or approved supply chain. Each production step depends on evidence and actual site permissions.</p><div class="bp-grid three">{concept.factory.map((cell,i)=><article class="bp-card"><p class="bp-number">CELL.{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</p><h3>{cell.name}</h3><p>{cell.body}</p></article>)}</div><p><a href="/manufacturing/">Explore the regional capability directory →</a></p><p class="bp-small">A public capability is a lead for qualification. It is not a supplier commitment, aerospace approval or an endorsement.</p></section>
  <section class="bp-section" id="roadmap"><p class="bp-number">04 / Research & capital architecture</p><h2>Fund the next question.</h2><p>2030 is a decision horizon. Dates below are illustrative planning hypotheses; each gate can delay, redirect or stop the program. Financing ideas describe R&D planning only.</p><div class="bp-grid">{concept.phases.map(phase=><article class="bp-card"><p class="bp-kicker">{phase.period}</p><h3>{phase.goal}</h3><dl><dt>Deliverable</dt><dd>{phase.deliverable}</dd><dt>Go / no-go gate</dt><dd>{phase.gate}</dd><dt>Planning assumption</dt><dd>{phase.budget}</dd><dt>Possible research support</dt><dd>{phase.funding}</dd></dl></article>)}</div><p class="bp-small">{concept.budgetNotes}</p><p class="bp-notice">This is an informational research roadmap. No investment terms, returns, funds collection or investment invitation are provided. Any actual capital-raising plan needs qualified securities counsel and a lawful offering route before public terms or solicitation. <a href={source('R20').url}>{source('R20').title}</a>.</p></section>
  <section class="bp-section" id="approval"><p class="bp-number">05 / The approvals are separate</p><h2>A form is not an aircraft category.</h2><div class="bp-grid">{regulatory.paths.map(path=><article class="bp-card"><h3>{path.label}</h3><p>{path.first_milestone}</p><ul class="bp-list">{path.regulatory_tracks.map(track=><li>{track}</li>)}</ul><p class="bp-small">Research judgment: {path.relative_execution_risk}. No eligibility is established for the rendered designs.</p>{path.sources.map(id=><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source(id).url}>{source(id).title} ↗</a>)}</article>)}<article class="bp-card"><h3>The 2026 MOSAIC fork</h3><p>Eligible two-seat powered-lift can have a light-sport special-airworthiness route under Part 22 / §21.190. A special-class type-certification route is a separate branch. Neither is assumed for these shapes.</p><p>The July 2026 acceptance of ASTM F3840-26 covered powered-lift only at that time, despite its title including multicopters. A generic wingless multicopter must not be treated as automatically eligible.</p><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R04').url}>MOSAIC final rule ↗</a><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R06').url}>Accepted standards, footnote 1 ↗</a><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R07').url}>FAA special-class guidance ↗</a></article></div><div class="bp-grid" style="margin-top:18px"><article class="bp-card"><h3>People & operations</h3><p>Light-sport aircraft certification does not create powered-lift sport-pilot privileges or general paid-passenger authority. The framework addressed here assumes onboard pilots; autonomous passenger service is not established.</p><p>SFAR 120 / Part 194 covers pilot training and operations separately. Experimental authorization does not grant routine commercial passenger permission; two occupants do not qualify as a Part 103 single-occupant ultralight.</p><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R09').url}>FAA powered-lift FAQ ↗</a><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R08').url}>Training and operations rule ↗</a><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R10').url}>Commercial operator certification ↗</a></article><article class="bp-card"><h3>Place & community</h3><p>Aircraft approval does not approve a landing site. LAX airspace, FAA review, Caltrans heliport permits, local land use, environmental review and emergency access need site-specific work. No speculative flight corridor or rooftop is approved here.</p><p>Electric imagery does not resolve noise, downwash, fire response or community acceptance. The proposed factory also requires parcel-level review.</p><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R14').url}>FAA airspace guidance ↗</a><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R15').url}>FAA infrastructure guidance ↗</a><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R17').url}>Caltrans heliport permits ↗</a><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={source('R19').url}>El Segundo General Plan ↗</a></article></div></section>
  <section class="bp-section"><p class="bp-number">06 / Questions worth keeping open</p><h2>The blueprint includes a stop button.</h2><ul class="bp-list">{concept.openQuestions.map(q=><li>{q}</li>)}</ul><p>Next useful work: define one civil ground-use case, commission qualified classification and safety review, and gather scoped nonflight prototype quotes. An independent review should be able to conclude that the aviation branch should stop.</p></section>
  <section class="bp-section" id="sources"><p class="bp-number">07 / Research record</p><h2>Sources & limits.</h2><p>Primary-source research checked {concept.checkedDate}. The architecture and roadmap are an original planning synthesis, not agency forecasts or legal advice. Direct eCFR retrieval and the final powered-lift safety-continuum policy were not independently verified in this research; no quantitative safety targets are claimed.</p><details class="bp-card"><summary>Open all {regulatory.sources.length} regulatory sources</summary>{regulatory.sources.map(s=><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={s.url}>{s.id} / {s.title} · checked {s.checked}</a>)}</details><p><a href="/mobility-2030.json">Download the concept and regulatory research JSON</a> · <a href="/mobility-2030-research/mobility-regulatory.md">Full readable regulatory brief</a></p></section>
  <footer class="bp-footer">PointCast / Hoydich Enterprises 2030 design study · Updated {concept.checkedDate}<br/>Original concept art and non-dimensional illustrations. <a href="/manufacturing/">Regional manufacturing atlas</a> · <a href="/">Return to PointCast</a></footer>
</div>
</BlockLayout>
